exports[`CLI help interface for 'config-manager delete cors' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo config-manager delete cors [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Experimental] Delete CORS configurations.

Arguments:
  host                AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am. To use
                      a connection profile, just specify a unique substring or
                      alias.
  realm               Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or 'realm'
                      or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default: "alpha" for
                      Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username            Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                      appropriate rights to manage authentication
                      journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                      matches the username already stored in the connection
                      profile for the target host, frodo uses that profile's
                      stored password instead of requiring it on the command
                      line.
  password            Password.

Options:
  --allow-failures    Report operations that fail, but still exit with code 0.
                      Without this option the command runs every operation,
                      prints a summary of what failed and exits with code 1.
  -d, --dry-run       Show what would be deleted or reset, without changing
                      anything.
  --deep              Also reset the IDM CORS filter to its default values
                      (Cloud and ForgeOps; a classic deployment has none).
                      Nothing is deleted by this option. Cannot be used with -i.
  -i, --cors-id <id>  CORS configuration id (its name, for example cors); delete
                      only that configuration. If omitted, all named CORS
                      configurations are deleted. (alias: -n, --name)
  -y, --yes           Do not ask for confirmation before deleting all CORS
                      configurations (no -i). Required without a terminal.
  -h, --help          Help
  -hh, --help-more    Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all    Help with all options, environment variables, and usage
                      examples.
"
`;
